    "Members from the sheet's หมายเหตุ legend: dash-dot line = อะเส 2C-150x50x20x3.2 mm., post marker = ตั้ง 2C-150x50x20x3.2 mm. The plan is the +4.09 layer (ระดับหลังอะเส): every dash-dot line is recorded as drawn, split at the 9 columns (small squares at A1, A2, A3, B1, B2, B3, C3, D1, D2).",
    "Three of the dash-dot lines are not wall plates but the bottom chords of the trusses — grid 2 (T1), A''' (T2, the ridge line) and 1'' (T3); the T1/T2/T3 elevations label their bottom chord 'อะเส 2C-150x50x20x3.2 mm.'. They carry truss_bottom_chord:<mark>. The truss elements on S-04 include these chords, so a consumer summing steel must not add both. Grid 2 between C and D is both the outer plate of the L and part of T1's chord — recorded once, inside B2-D2.",
    "T2's chord bears on the grid-1 and grid-3 plates at A''' (0.25 short of columns B1/B3); T3's chord runs from T2 (A'''1'') to the row-D plate at D1'' (no column there).",
    "Posts (ตั้ง): 11 markers — on grid 2 at 1.25 / 2.50 / 3.75 / 5.00 / 6.25 from A, on A''' at 2.00 / 6.00 from grid 1, on 1'' at 4.66 / 5.58 / 6.50 / 7.50 from A. They sit exactly on the T1/T2/T3 panel points, but those panel chains are printed only on the truss elevations with no grid markers (floating, section 4 rule 4), so the entry carries the three member lines as ranges, not point refs.",
    "Spec conflict, decided: the S-03 legend calls the posts 2C-150x50x20x3.2, while the truss elevations (same sheet and S-04) print the verticals as 2C-100x50x20x3.2 (T1, T2) and C-100x50x20x3.2 (T3). Detail beats plan (op01 precedence 2): the member spec lives on the truss section files; the post entry keeps only this sheet's legend text in printed_as, flagged."
